{"bubbleSort":{"title":"Bubble Sort","level":"beginner","steps":[{"step":1,"concept":"Introduction and Setup","subtitle":"Let's learn how bubble sort works by sorting a small list of numbers. Our example list is 5, 3, 8, and 4. Bubble sort compares pairs of numbers and swaps them if they are in the wrong order. This process repeats until the whole list is sorted.","duration_ms":18800,"canvas_instructions":{"elements":[{"type":"text","x":10,"y":10,"width":80,"height":8,"color":"#64748b","label":"Bubble sort compares pairs","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":20,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#ff6b35","label":"5","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":1000,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":36,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#ff6b35","label":"3","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":1200,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":52,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#00d4ff","label":"8","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":1400,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":68,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#00d4ff","label":"4","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":1600,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"highlight_box","x":18,"y":38,"width":34,"height":24,"color":"#ff6b35","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"pulse","duration":900,"delay":1800,"direction":"none"},"label":""},{"type":"text","x":10,"y":70,"width":80,"height":8,"color":"#64748b","label":"Example list 5 3","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":700,"delay":2000,"direction":"none"}}]}},{"step":2,"concept":"First Comparison and Swap","subtitle":"We start by comparing the first two numbers: 5 and 3. Since 5 is greater than 3, we swap their positions. Now the list looks like 3, 5, 8, 4. This is the first step in moving larger numbers towards the end of the list.","duration_ms":18000,"canvas_instructions":{"elements":[{"type":"rectangle","x":20,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#00D4FF","label":"5","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"none","duration":1200,"delay":4000,"direction":"none","target_x":36,"target_y":40}},{"type":"rectangle","x":36,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#FF6B35","label":"3","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"none","duration":1200,"delay":4000,"direction":"none","target_x":20,"target_y":40}},{"type":"rectangle","x":52,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#00d4ff","label":"8","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":68,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#00d4ff","label":"4","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"highlight_box","x":18,"y":38,"width":34,"height":24,"color":"#facc15","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"pulse","duration":900,"delay":3500,"direction":"none"},"label":""},{"type":"text","x":10,"y":10,"width":80,"height":10,"color":"#00D4FF","label":"Compare and swap 5","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"text","x":10,"y":75,"width":80,"height":10,"color":"#00D4FF","label":"Swap since 5  3","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":3500,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"text","x":10,"y":85,"width":80,"height":10,"color":"#00D4FF","label":"List after swap 3","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":5500,"direction":"none"}}]}},{"step":3,"concept":"Second Comparison","subtitle":"Next, we compare the second and third numbers: 5 and 8. Since 5 is less than 8, we do not swap them. The list remains 3, 5, 8, 4. This means the larger number 8 stays in place for now.","duration_ms":16000,"canvas_instructions":{"elements":[{"type":"rectangle","x":20,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#00d4ff","label":"3","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":36,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#FF6B35","label":"5","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":400,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":52,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#00D4FF","label":"8","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":400,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":68,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#00d4ff","label":"4","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"highlight_box","x":34,"y":38,"width":34,"height":24,"color":"#facc15","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"pulse","duration":900,"delay":1000,"direction":"none"},"label":""},{"type":"text","x":20,"y":10,"width":60,"height":10,"color":"#00D4FF","label":"Compare 5 and 8","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":700,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}}]}},{"step":4,"concept":"Third Comparison and Swap","subtitle":"Then, we compare the third and fourth numbers: 8 and 4. Since 8 is greater than 4, we swap them. The list updates to 3, 5, 4, 8. Now, the largest number 8 has moved to the end of the list.","duration_ms":16400,"canvas_instructions":{"elements":[{"type":"rectangle","x":20,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#00d4ff","label":"3","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":36,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#00d4ff","label":"5","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":52,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#FF6B35","label":"8","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"none","duration":1200,"delay":3000,"direction":"none","target_x":66,"target_y":40}},{"type":"rectangle","x":66,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#00D4FF","label":"4","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"none","duration":1200,"delay":3000,"direction":"none","target_x":52,"target_y":40}},{"type":"highlight_box","x":50,"y":35,"width":32,"height":30,"color":"#facc15","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"pulse","duration":900,"delay":2500,"direction":"none"},"label":""},{"type":"text","x":20,"y":10,"width":60,"height":10,"color":"#00D4FF","label":"Compare 8 and 4","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"text","x":66,"y":65,"width":14,"height":6,"color":"#FF6B35","label":"8 at end","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":4500,"direction":"none"}}]}},{"step":5,"concept":"Second Pass Begins","subtitle":"We start the second pass by comparing the first two numbers again: 3 and 5. Since 3 is less than 5, no swap is needed. The list stays 3, 5, 4, 8. This pass helps to sort the remaining unsorted numbers.","duration_ms":16400,"canvas_instructions":{"elements":[{"type":"rectangle","x":20,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#FF6B35","label":"3","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":36,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#00D4FF","label":"5","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":52,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#00d4ff","label":"4","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":68,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#00d4ff","label":"8","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"highlight_box","x":18,"y":38,"width":34,"height":24,"color":"#ff6b35","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"pulse","duration":900,"delay":1000,"direction":"none"},"label":""},{"type":"text","x":20,"y":15,"width":60,"height":10,"color":"#00D4FF","label":"Compare 3 and 5","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"text","x":20,"y":70,"width":60,"height":10,"color":"#00D4FF","label":"List remains 3 5","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":1600,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"text","x":20,"y":80,"width":60,"height":10,"color":"#64748b","label":"Pass sorts remaining numbers","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":2200,"direction":"none"}}]}},{"step":6,"concept":"Second Pass Swap","subtitle":"Next, we compare 5 and 4. Since 5 is greater than 4, we swap them. The list becomes 3, 4, 5, 8. Now, the smaller numbers are moving towards the front, and the list is almost sorted.","duration_ms":14800,"canvas_instructions":{"elements":[{"type":"rectangle","x":20,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#00d4ff","label":"3","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":36,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#FF6B35","label":"5","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"none","duration":1200,"delay":4000,"direction":"none","target_x":50,"target_y":40}},{"type":"rectangle","x":50,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#00D4FF","label":"4","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"none","duration":1200,"delay":4000,"direction":"none","target_x":36,"target_y":40}},{"type":"rectangle","x":64,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#00d4ff","label":"8","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"highlight_box","x":34,"y":38,"width":32,"height":24,"color":"#facc15","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"pulse","duration":900,"delay":4000,"direction":"none"},"label":""},{"type":"text","x":20,"y":10,"width":60,"height":10,"color":"#00D4FF","label":"Compare and swap 5","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"text","x":20,"y":70,"width":60,"height":10,"color":"#00D4FF","label":"List becomes 3 4","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":5500,"direction":"none"}}]}},{"step":7,"concept":"Final Pass and Completion","subtitle":"In the final pass, we compare 3 and 4, and then 4 and 5. Both pairs are in the correct order, so no swaps happen. The list is now fully sorted as 3, 4, 5, 8. Bubble sort finishes when no swaps are needed in a pass.","duration_ms":18800,"canvas_instructions":{"elements":[{"type":"text","x":10,"y":10,"width":80,"height":8,"color":"#64748b","label":"Final pass compare pairs","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":20,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#FF6B35","label":"3","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"highlight","duration":1000,"delay":1000,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":36,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#00D4FF","label":"4","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"highlight","duration":1000,"delay":1000,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":52,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#ff6b35","label":"5","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"highlight","duration":1000,"delay":3000,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":68,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#00d4ff","label":"8","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"highlight_box","x":18,"y":38,"width":32,"height":24,"color":"#facc15","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"pulse","duration":900,"delay":1000,"direction":"none"},"label":""},{"type":"highlight_box","x":50,"y":38,"width":32,"height":24,"color":"#facc15","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"pulse","duration":900,"delay":3000,"direction":"none"},"label":""},{"type":"text","x":10,"y":75,"width":80,"height":10,"color":"#00D4FF","label":"List fully sorted 3","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":1000,"delay":5000,"direction":"none"}}]}},{"step":8,"concept":"Summary and Importance","subtitle":"Bubble sort is simple but not very fast for large lists because it compares many pairs repeatedly. It works well for small or nearly sorted lists. Understanding bubble sort helps build a foundation for learning more efficient sorting methods.","duration_ms":15600,"canvas_instructions":{"elements":[{"type":"rectangle","x":20,"y":40,"width":14,"height":20,"color":"#22c55e","label":"3","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":36,"y":40,"width":14,"height":30,"color":"#22c55e","label":"4","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":200,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":52,"y":40,"width":14,"height":25,"color":"#22c55e","label":"5","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":400,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":68,"y":40,"width":14,"height":35,"color":"#22c55e","label":"8","label_position":"below","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":600,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"text","x":20,"y":75,"width":60,"height":8,"color":"#64748b","label":"Simple but slow for","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":1000,"delay":1000,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"circle","x":85,"y":55,"width":12,"height":10,"color":"#facc15","label":"Concept","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":1200,"direction":"none"},"radius":6},{"type":"stack","x":80,"y":70,"width":12,"height":20,"color":"#00d4ff","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":1400,"direction":"none"},"values":["...","...","..."],"label":"bubble 7"},{"type":"text","x":10,"y":10,"width":80,"height":10,"color":"#8b5cf6","label":"Understanding bubble sort builds","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":1200,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}}]}}]},"tcpHandshake":{"title":"How TCP three-way handshake works","level":"beginner","steps":[{"step":1,"concept":"Connection Initiation","subtitle":"Let's say Alice's computer wants to connect to Bob's server at IP 192.168.1.10 on port 80. Alice's computer picks an initial sequence number, 1000, to start the communication. This sequence number helps both sides keep track of the data they send and receive. The connection begins with Alice sending a special packet called SYN to Bob.","duration_ms":22400,"canvas_instructions":{"elements":[{"type":"rectangle","x":10,"y":30,"width":20,"height":25,"color":"#00d4ff","label":"Alice (Client)","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":70,"y":30,"width":25,"height":25,"color":"#8b5cf6","label":"Bob (Server 192.168.1.1080)","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":400,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"arrow","x":50,"y":50,"x1":30,"y1":42,"x2":70,"y2":42,"width":18,"height":2,"color":"#ff6b35","label":"","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"draw","duration":1200,"delay":1000,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":45,"y":35,"width":15,"height":10,"color":"#ff6b35","label":"SYN Flag","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"pulse","duration":1000,"delay":1300,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"text","x":5,"y":10,"width":90,"height":10,"color":"#64748b","label":"Alice initiates connection with","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"typewriter","duration":1500,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}}]}},{"step":2,"concept":"SYN Packet Sent","subtitle":"Alice sends the SYN packet with sequence number 1000 to Bob. This packet signals Alice's intent to start a connection and tells Bob where Alice will begin counting bytes. Bob receives this SYN and prepares to respond. The SYN flag is set to indicate this is a connection request, not data.","duration_ms":20400,"canvas_instructions":{"elements":[{"type":"rectangle","x":10,"y":40,"width":20,"height":20,"color":"#00d4ff","label":"Alice (Client)","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":70,"y":40,"width":25,"height":20,"color":"#8b5cf6","label":"Bob (Server 192.168.1.1080)","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"arrow","x":50,"y":50,"x1":30,"y1":50,"x2":70,"y2":50,"width":18,"height":2,"color":"#ff6b35","label":"","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"draw","duration":1200,"delay":1000,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":55,"y":65,"width":35,"height":10,"color":"#ff6b35","label":"SYN flag set","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"highlight","duration":1000,"delay":1500,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"text","x":70,"y":35,"width":25,"height":10,"color":"#8b5cf6","label":"Received SYN Seq1000","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":2000,"direction":"none"}}]}},{"step":3,"concept":"SYN-ACK Response","subtitle":"Bob replies with a SYN-ACK packet to Alice. This packet has two important parts: a SYN flag with Bob's own initial sequence number, say 2000, and an ACK flag acknowledging Alice's sequence number 1001. The acknowledgment number is Alice's sequence number plus one, confirming he received the SYN.","duration_ms":19200,"canvas_instructions":{"elements":[{"type":"rectangle","x":10,"y":30,"width":20,"height":20,"color":"#00d4ff","label":"Bob (Server 192.168.1.1080)","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":70,"y":30,"width":20,"height":20,"color":"#8b5cf6","label":"Alice (Client)","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"arrow","x":50,"y":50,"x1":20,"y1":40,"x2":80,"y2":40,"width":18,"height":2,"color":"#ff6b35","label":"","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"draw","duration":1200,"delay":1000,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"text","x":35,"y":10,"width":30,"height":6,"color":"#ff6b35","label":"Bob sends SYN-ACK","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":15,"y":60,"width":20,"height":12,"color":"#ff6b35","label":"Seq2000","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":1500,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":15,"y":75,"width":20,"height":12,"color":"#ff6b35","label":"Ack1001","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":1800,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":75,"y":60,"width":20,"height":12,"color":"#8b5cf6","label":"Seq1001","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":2000,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":75,"y":75,"width":20,"height":12,"color":"#00d4ff","label":"Ack2000","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"none","duration":1000,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"text","x":40,"y":80,"width":20,"height":6,"color":"#ff6b35","label":"SYN and ACK flags","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"highlight","duration":800,"delay":1200,"direction":"none"}}]}},{"step":4,"concept":"ACK from Client","subtitle":"Alice sends back an ACK packet to Bob. This packet acknowledges Bob's sequence number by setting the acknowledgment number to 2001, which is Bob's sequence number plus one. The ACK flag is set, and no SYN flag is needed here. This completes Alice's side of the handshake.","duration_ms":18800,"canvas_instructions":{"elements":[{"type":"rectangle","x":10,"y":30,"width":20,"height":20,"color":"#00d4ff","label":"Alice (Client)","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":70,"y":30,"width":20,"height":20,"color":"#8b5cf6","label":"Bob (Server 192.168.1.1080)","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"arrow","x":50,"y":50,"x1":30,"y1":40,"x2":70,"y2":40,"width":18,"height":2,"color":"#ff6b35","label":"","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"draw","duration":1200,"delay":1000,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"text","x":10,"y":55,"width":20,"height":6,"color":"#ff6b35","label":"Seq  1001","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":500,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"text","x":10,"y":62,"width":20,"height":6,"color":"#ff6b35","label":"Ack  2001","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":500,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"text","x":70,"y":55,"width":20,"height":6,"color":"#8b5cf6","label":"Seq  2000","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"text","x":70,"y":62,"width":20,"height":6,"color":"#8b5cf6","label":"Ack  1001","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"highlight_box","x":30,"y":35,"width":40,"height":10,"color":"#ff6b35","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"pulse","duration":1000,"delay":1000,"direction":"none"},"label":""},{"type":"text","x":25,"y":10,"width":50,"height":8,"color":"#64748b","label":"ACK from Client","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"text","x":30,"y":25,"width":40,"height":8,"color":"#ff6b35","label":"ACK flag set no","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":1200,"direction":"none"}}]}},{"step":5,"concept":"Connection Established","subtitle":"At this point, both Alice and Bob have acknowledged each other's sequence numbers. The three-way handshake is complete, and the connection is established. Now, they can start exchanging actual data securely and reliably. This handshake ensures both sides are synchronized and ready to communicate.","duration_ms":17600,"canvas_instructions":{"elements":[{"type":"rectangle","x":14,"y":26,"width":24,"height":12,"color":"#4A90E2","label":"point both Alice Bob","label_position":"above","animation":{}},{"type":"rectangle","x":44,"y":26,"width":24,"height":12,"color":"#00D4FF","label":"three-way handshake complete connection","label_position":"above","animation":{}},{"type":"rectangle","x":74,"y":26,"width":18,"height":12,"color":"#8B5CF6","label":"Now start exchanging actual","label_position":"above","animation":{}},{"type":"arrow","x1":38,"y1":32,"x2":44,"y2":32,"width":1,"height":1,"color":"#9db2ce","label":"","label_position":"above","animation":{}},{"type":"arrow","x1":68,"y1":32,"x2":74,"y2":32,"width":1,"height":1,"color":"#9db2ce","label":"","label_position":"above","animation":{}},{"type":"text","x":16,"y":12,"width":28,"height":6,"color":"#d9e6ff","label":"handshake ensures both sides","label_position":"right","animation":{}}]}},{"step":6,"concept":"Why Three-Way Handshake","subtitle":"The three-way handshake prevents old or duplicate connection requests from causing confusion. It synchronizes sequence numbers so both sides agree on where data starts. This process also confirms that both computers are ready to communicate. Although it adds a small delay, it ensures reliable and ordered data transfer over TCP.","duration_ms":20000,"canvas_instructions":{"elements":[{"type":"text","x":10,"y":8,"width":80,"height":6,"color":"#ff6b35","label":"Why Three-Way Handshake","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":15,"y":30,"width":20,"height":12,"color":"#00d4ff","label":"SYN Seq1000","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":500,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":55,"y":30,"width":30,"height":12,"color":"#8b5cf6","label":"SYN-ACK Seq2000 Ack1001","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":1900,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":15,"y":45,"width":20,"height":12,"color":"#22c55e","label":"ACK Seq1001 Ack2001","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":3400,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"highlight_box","x":14,"y":28,"width":72,"height":32,"color":"#facc15","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"pulse","duration":1200,"delay":4000,"direction":"none"},"label":""},{"type":"text","x":10,"y":65,"width":80,"height":8,"color":"#facc15","label":"Prevents duplicates ensures reliability","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"typewriter","duration":1200,"delay":5200,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"circle","x":85,"y":70,"width":12,"height":10,"color":"#64748b","label":"Concept","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":6500,"direction":"none"},"radius":6},{"type":"text","x":75,"y":78,"width":20,"height":6,"color":"#64748b","label":"Small delay added","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":600,"delay":7000,"direction":"none"}}]}}]},"softmax":{"title":"Softmax Function","level":"beginner","steps":[{"step":1,"concept":"Introduction to Softmax","subtitle":"Let's explore the softmax function using a simple example. Imagine we have three scores: 2, 1, and 0. These scores could represent how confident a model is about three different choices. Softmax will help us turn these scores into probabilities that add up to 1.","duration_ms":18000,"canvas_instructions":{"elements":[{"type":"text","x":10,"y":10,"width":80,"height":10,"color":"#64748b","label":"Lets explore the softmax","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":1000,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":15,"y":40,"width":20,"height":20,"color":"#ff6b35","label":"Score 1 2","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":1200,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":42,"y":40,"width":20,"height":20,"color":"#ff6b35","label":"Score 2 1","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":1400,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":69,"y":40,"width":20,"height":20,"color":"#ff6b35","label":"Score 3 0","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":1600,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"text","x":10,"y":70,"width":80,"height":10,"color":"#64748b","label":"These scores represent model","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":1800,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"text","x":10,"y":82,"width":80,"height":10,"color":"#64748b","label":"Softmax turns scores into","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":2000,"direction":"none"}}]}},{"step":2,"concept":"Exponentiate Scores","subtitle":"The first step in softmax is to exponentiate each score. This means raising the number e to the power of each score. For our scores, e^2 is about 7.39, e^1 is about 2.72, and e^0 is 1. This step makes all numbers positive and emphasizes larger scores.","duration_ms":18800,"canvas_instructions":{"elements":[{"type":"rectangle","x":15,"y":40,"width":20,"height":15,"color":"#00d4ff","label":"Score 1 2","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":0,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":42,"y":40,"width":20,"height":15,"color":"#00d4ff","label":"Score 2 1","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":200,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":69,"y":40,"width":20,"height":15,"color":"#00d4ff","label":"Score 3 0","label_position":"above","animation":{"type":"fade_in","duration":800,"delay":400,"direction":"none"}},{"type":"rectangle","x":15,"y":65,"width":20,"height":15,"color":"#ff